tion payload. Generated when omitted and returned with the result.', 'type': 'string', 'pattern': '^[A-Za-z0-9._:-]{1,128}$'}, 'alexandria': {'description': 'Catalogued Alexandria capability invocation, mutually exclusive with url. One {provider, capability, options} object or an array of 1-10, with contracts available through firecrawl_search or firecrawl_find_tools. Each call may include version to pin a published workflow; omitting it uses latest. Only requestId and timeout are supported alongside alexandria. The selected contract marks required inputs and any requiresOneOf groups (at least one member per group); it may include example.request/example.response and response.key (which may differ from records). Where pagination is declared, its fields govern paging with the same filters; catalogue next is separate from provider pagination. Returns per-capability results in data.alexandria with data, records, or an error with a code; individual capabilities can fail even when the outer response succeeds. Some providers require accepted terms; when a response reports a terms requirement, direct the user to the Firecrawl dashboard URL in that response.', 'anyOf': [{'type': 'object', 'properties': {'provider': {'description': 'Provider slug, e.g. "fred".', 'type': 'string', 'minLength': 1}, 'capability': {'description': 'Capability address as returned by search or discover, e.g. "series/observations".', 'type': 'string', 'minLength': 1}, 'version': {'description': 'Optional published workflow version. Omit to use the latest version.', 'type': 'string', 'minLength': 1, 'maxLength': 128}, 'options': {'description': 'Capability options as declared by its contract.', 'type': 'object', 'propertyNames': {'type': 'string'}, 'additionalProperties': {}}}, 'required': ['provider', 'capability']}, {'minItems': 1, 'maxItems': 10, 'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'provider': {'description': 'Provider slug, e.g. "fred".', 'type': 'string', 'minLength': 1},